 ## MVP Scope
 
@@ -96,6 +96,23 @@ ### Ticket
 
 **Issuance:** domain action `App\Actions\IssueTicket` rejects inactive queues (`is_active = false`), requires `priority >= 0`, allocates the next code, and creates a ticket with `status=waiting` and `issued_at` set.
 
+### Queue management and who may call
+
+Authorization lives in `App\Policies\QueuePolicy` (single source of truth); domain writes go through `App\Actions\CreateQueue`, `UpdateQueue` and `SetQueueAccess`. There is no UI yet.
+
+| Ability | Who |
+| ------- | --- |
+| `create` (entity), `update`, `manageAccess` | Owner/admin of the queue's entity only. Employees, members of other entities and non-members get `AuthorizationException` and nothing is written. |
+| `call` | Owner/admin of the queue's entity always (no grant row needed). An employee only with a `queue_access` row for **that** queue whose `permissions` is an array containing `call` (a corrupted non-array value denies). Everyone else is denied. |
+
+- **Create:** name is trimmed, 1–255 characters; slug defaults to `Str::slug(name)`, an explicit slug is slugified too; new queues are active.
+- **Slug uniqueness:** unique **per entity** (the same slug may exist in another entity). A duplicate — including one caught by the unique index in a race — is a `ValidationException`.
+- **Update:** any combination of name, slug and active flag; `null` leaves a field unchanged; keeping the queue's own slug is fine.
+- **No hard delete:** a queue is retired by deactivating it (`is_active = false`). Its tickets are preserved, and issuing or calling on it fails with `InactiveQueueException`. No delete/remove/destroy action exists.
+- **Access grants:** a manager sets the permissions of a membership on a queue; a non-empty list upserts the `queue_access` row, an empty list revokes (deletes) it. The only permission is `call` (`App\Enums\QueuePermission`). Unknown or non-string entries, or a membership and queue of different entities, are a `ValidationException` and nothing is stored. Employees cannot grant themselves access.
+- **Audit:** grants and revokes are logged on the `audit` channel as `queue.access.granted` / `queue.access.revoked` with `actor_id`, `queue_id` and `entity_membership_id`; a revoke with no row to delete is not logged.
+- **Calling:** both `CallNextTicket` (every call mode) and `Ticket::call()` lock the queue, reject inactive queues (`InactiveQueueException`), then authorize `call` (`AuthorizationException`, even if the ticket was already called) before the "only waiting tickets" check.
+
 **Immutability enforcement:** the write-once rule is enforced on the `Ticket` model (`updating` hook), so it applies to Eloquent saves only — mass updates through the query builder (`Ticket::query()->update(...)`) bypass it and must not be used on issued tickets.
 
 **Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (entity-membership checked, exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields. Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it); AuthZ stays out of scope per #20 and HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
