 | **Owner invariant** | `entity_memberships` has exactly one `role='owner'` per `entity_id`. Enforced by `entities.owner_seq` (generated `CASE WHEN role='owner' THEN 1 ELSE NULL END`) + unique `(entity_id, owner_seq)` — permits multiple non-owners, rejects a 2nd owner. No FK back to `entities`. Ownership transfer = demote old owner (role→admin), promote target admin (role→owner); the generated column + unique index tolerate the transient no-owner row within the transaction. |
 | `entity_memberships.role` | enum | `admin`, `owner`, `employee` — billing only for owner |
 | `plans` → limits | — | `max_users`, `max_queues` |
-| `queue_access` | join 1:N/1:N | Employee: granular permissions per queue |
+| `queue_access` | join 1:N/1:N | Employee: granular permissions per queue. `entity_membership_id` and `queue_id` are FKs with `ON DELETE CASCADE`; `permissions` is a JSON array of strings (only `call` today); unique `(entity_membership_id, queue_id)`. A row exists only while at least one permission is granted — revoking deletes it. Membership and queue must belong to the same entity (enforced by `SetQueueAccess`, not by the schema). |
 | `queues` → `tickets` | 1 : N | Ticket belongs to **one** queue; ordering by `priority` (desc) + `issued_at` (asc) |
 | `users` → `tickets` | 1 : N | `called_by_user_id`: attendant who called the ticket |
 | `totems` | per entity | Device registration for API auth; **no** ticket relationship |
